Questions and crossings across philosophy (@greek-question-crossings: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @ancient-greek-philosophy, #contains @greek-comparative-inquiry, #philosophy @greek-comparative-inquiry, #ancient-greek-philosophy @greek-comparative-inquiry) { r_1KWY32YG72JSYZZEYW3GH6W0XF
Use a question to move between readings. Each crossing explains the shared problem; the destination guide introduces its own preparation.

| Question or method | Start and continue | What to examine across the boundary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| What makes a claim, definition, or inference defensible? | [Euthyphro](../socratic/Euthyphro.lingua#r_2B4XJJ3N8YSZ35JXZCV51QTRBD) → [Parmenides](../presocratics/Parmenides.lingua#r_7HVRAJY7AF3178NEH1N8BF9NPV) → [Aristotle's logical works](../aristotle/Logic-and-demonstration.lingua#r_1SRR6TVQ8CC029F7QK6PKPM1X9) | Definition, consequence, contradiction, and the assumptions of a general account |
| What distinguishes knowledge from correct opinion? | [Meno](../socratic/Meno.lingua#r_6NC59NWAQ6A7YZYBJ3CG12SCTN) → [Theaetetus](../plato/Theaetetus.lingua#r_3T0C5M7DVRZDE4ENZ3Z0V0AV2N) → [demonstration](../aristotle/Logic-and-demonstration.lingua#r_1SRR6TVQ8CC029F7QK6PKPM1X9) → [the sceptics](../schools/Sceptics.lingua#r_6KEA1AHWJRDT3ZN8VJQTK06ZFK) | The grounds of a claim, learning, disagreement, and criteria for accepting an answer |
| What should guide a decision? | [Crito](../socratic/Crito.lingua#r_54N10WGKCSCKW6XM202PCG7ZDH) → [Aristotle](../aristotle/Practical-wisdom-and-friendship.lingua#r_6RZXS4EJH55PRPW61MB33DTCNM) → [Epictetus](../schools/Epictetus.lingua#r_35EWPVCFYNWZ0DYG5R5HM05TC2) | Obligation, deliberation, character, agency, and the particulars of a situation |
| What makes a life good? | [Gorgias](../socratic/Gorgias.lingua#r_5G884J0SFXCP4YRBFF5C5YSYD2) → [Aristotle](../aristotle/Living-well-and-character.lingua#r_21YB00AWNRYQ0X2SQ8H0RFRW65) → [Epicurus](../schools/Epicurus.lingua#r_6KHZKEFRKY1J18Z7TSRAJABZQP) | Competing ends, desire, virtue, pleasure, and arguments for their value |
| What are soul, reality, and change? | [Heraclitus](../presocratics/Heraclitus.lingua#r_5K10CZBC41P0MXC7M3M1NW8MKY) → [Parmenides](../presocratics/Parmenides.lingua#r_7HVRAJY7AF3178NEH1N8BF9NPV) → [Phaedo](../plato/Phaedo.lingua#r_6JFZZP5W43FY7FFQENQNH96AFQ) | Persistence, intelligibility, explanation, and the difference between an analogy and a demonstration |
| What can number and division explain? | [The Pythagoreans](../presocratics/Pythagoreans.lingua#r_2J6KPA7CCD3NY1G0VCAT35Q2NK) → [Zeno and Melissus](../presocratics/Zeno-and-Melissus.lingua#r_5WR6CJM0JV5QPDX2P5177J0YT4) → [Meno](../socratic/Meno.lingua#r_6NC59NWAQ6A7YZYBJ3CG12SCTN) | Quantitative description, arguments about plurality or motion, and the basis of a mathematical demonstration |
| What supports a claim about the divine? | [Xenophanes](../presocratics/Xenophanes.lingua#r_7R4H94PKX5S41NDVCJSZE0N88B) → [Euthyphro](../socratic/Euthyphro.lingua#r_2B4XJJ3N8YSZ35JXZCV51QTRBD) | Human representations, reasons for approval, evidence, and the limits of an inference |
| What kind of cause does an explanation offer? | [Empedocles](../presocratics/Empedocles.lingua#r_0JDEHV9WCX6YWPPXE64Z26VAMZ) → [Anaxagoras](../presocratics/Anaxagoras.lingua#r_2KMHNE6TG1NF6X3Q4SXMBHGWXN) → [Phaedo](../plato/Phaedo.lingua#r_6JFZZP5W43FY7FFQENQNH96AFQ) → [Aristotle](../aristotle/Nature-causes-and-being.lingua#r_2MGDMPK353BD8MFMFDMA3JPJ9P) | Constituents, mixture, order, physical conditions, purposes, and reasons for an outcome |
| How do love, beauty, and literary form shape inquiry? | [Symposium](../plato/Symposium.lingua#r_5NMHFGWX7QGRJ65XQDFFEG9K8B) → [Poetics](../aristotle/Poetry-and-representation.lingua#r_5PBR5GVV367JEK4PF94Q2YJKBE) → [Plotinus](../schools/Plotinus.lingua#r_375WTA2HXW04F1FC4FVW20B9N9) | Desire, representation, ascent, form, and reasons for preferring an interpretation |
| Who works, decides, and learns in a society? | [Protagoras](../socratic/Protagoras.lingua#r_6QKC211R791MTAMXSZM0VBS5XN) → [Republic](../plato/Republic.lingua#r_05G1N50PP71GRGDNAPG38CQ8J5) → [Politics](../aristotle/Political-community.lingua#r_0NZK4NKSQVX9NMTAWRT2XNBATD) → [the Cynics](../schools/Cynics.lingua#r_0R2YCT14QC77FB489JPCD107SZ) | Education, civic obligation, participation, material dependence, and the distribution of roles |
| What makes a historical claim credible? | [Socrates and his sources](../foundations/Socrates-and-his-sources.lingua#r_1WAA32AYYPKYVETNZ5JGZ2SHFT) → [Plato and Xenophon](../socratic/Xenophon.lingua#r_386T9BE05SXJZK8E0NX7TAYJK8) → [early Greek reports](../presocratics/Nature-and-being.lingua#r_61M87EN28QQ9AHXT80SPCB0CVH) | Provenance, genre, translation, agreement, survival of evidence, and uncertainty |

These questions also connect the study to mathematics, science, history, literature, social inquiry, and practical work. For mathematics, compare a geometrical demonstration in Meno with an argument about learning, identifying their different claims. For science or engineering, compare persuasion about a result with evidence and a justified explanation. For history, ask what the source can establish before using it as a fact about a person.

Take a concrete claim from another area and write the bridge: what is shared, what changes in meaning or standard of evidence, and what further preparation is required. A conceptual resemblance can open a question without proving an equivalence between fields.

**Practice:** [Develop one comparison](Comparative-investigation.lingua#r_20BK69Q76HJXAGZ5J1T097X29G). **Return:** [Ancient Greek philosophy](../Ancient-Greek-Philosophy.lingua#r_464ZHR7ZYC234A0XX2QEW47VB3) · [Philosophy](../../Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001).

**Across languages:** compare the same passage through [Portuguese and English editions](../sources/Portuguese-editions.lingua#r_3DABDPGKRDSM682Q2NYDEVX4Z8). For a supported investigation of the wording itself, follow [the Ancient Greek entrance](../languages/Read-original-texts.lingua#r_1Q07KPDNG2JTY7HRWQY5H6T5MJ).

**Research routes:** [The advanced families](../research/seminars/Seminars.lingua#r_5FTSQDJTR924S9Z0G9EDBQFR1Y) deepen these questions through full relevant works and scholarly debate. Use the same readings and notes wherever they help an investigation.
